      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for testing this. In your standalone build sdbusplus was built as a subproject, and the `if sdbusplus_dep.type_name() \u003d\u003d \u0027internal\u0027` / `subdir_done()` block at the top of this file then skipped all the checks. That block existed because cpp.compiles() rejects internal dependencies (\"Dependencies must be external dependencies\").\n\nThe next patch set removes the skip and passes `phosphor_logging_dep.partial_dependency(compile_args: true, includes: true)` instead, which Meson accepts in compiler checks because it has no link targets. With this change, corrupting the valid invocation makes `meson setup` fail with \"Assert failed: lg2: valid invocation did not compile\", including in a standalone build.\n\nNote: Meson caches compiler check results in the build directory. A change to the snippets themselves is always re-checked, but a change to the lg2 headers is only re-checked in an existing build directory after `meson setup --wipe` or `meson configure --clearcache`.",
